# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# prefs: factory
# setup: ideconnect
# board: discover
# Where a program goes is chosen in Connect, and the project remembers.
#
# A board is CONNECTED from the desktop's Devices menu before any of
# this: finding one on the bus no longer mounts it, choosing it does.
# Picking a board in Connect makes it that project's destination: Run
# reads as going there, and asking the shell to look again mounts
# nothing twice.
wait 200
note the two boards on the bench, taken in from the Devices menu
click 264 8
wait 10
menu-pick nRF54L15
wait 300
click 264 8
wait 10
menu-pick nRF54LM20B
wait 300
note and the desktop is current on THIS machine again, so a project
note that names no board still runs here until it says otherwise
click 264 8
wait 10
menu-pick This machine
wait 20
click 980 30
wait 10
menu-pick Programming
wait 10
menu-pick TikuBasic
wait 250
expect-title Project
click 71 8
wait 8
menu-pick Open Project…
wait 40
expect-title Open
click 400 220
wait 6
click 675 413
wait 60
expect-no-title Open
click-window Project
note the shell is looking for boards now, one port a beat -- and the
note desk is still a desk while it does: its menu opens at once
wait 10
click 71 8
wait 8
expect-menu New Project…|Open Project…||Run||Close Project|
click-window Project
wait 200
note runs go to this machine until a board is chosen
click 71 8
wait 8
expect-menu New Project…|Open Project…||Run||Close Project|
click-window Project
wait 10
note the boards the shell found when the project opened, and the one
note place a program can always go
click 175 8
wait 8
expect-menu This machine|nrf54l15|nrf54lm20b||Look again|
menu-pick nrf54lm20b
wait 10
note and now Run says where it will go
click 71 8
wait 8
expect-menu Run on nrf54lm20b|Save on nrf54lm20b|
click-window Project
wait 10
note looking again finds the same boards, not the same boards twice
click 175 8
wait 8
menu-pick Look again
wait 400
click 175 8
wait 8
expect-menu This machine|nrf54l15|nrf54lm20b||Look again|
quit
